{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_setup_setup", "label": "Setup - toolchain and build", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_setup_arm_gnu_toolchain", "label": "The ARM GNU bare-metal toolchain", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Toolchain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "aarch64-none-elf, downloaded from ARM's site: genuinely bare metal with no Linux assumptions, shipping gcc, binutils and gdb in one tarball with nothing to build."}, {"id": "docs_setup_default_is_the_machine_written_on", "label": "The default in an instruction should be the machine it was written on", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Toolchain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The commands used to say darwin-x86_64 with a note to swap it. Following them exactly gave a tarball that does not run; following them nearly exactly gave 'aarch64-none-elf-gcc: No such file or directory', which says the compiler is missing rather than that the path has the wrong architecture in it. An hour of a session went into that."}, {"id": "docs_setup_gatekeeper_quarantine", "label": "xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine is not optional", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Toolchain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "macOS quarantines anything downloaded through a browser or curl, and without clearing it Gatekeeper kills the binaries with a message that does not say why."}, {"id": "docs_setup_libm_dependency", "label": "The kernel needs a compiler; the userland needs a compiler and a libm", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Toolchain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Homebrew's aarch64-elf-gcc compiles the whole tree cleanly and cannot link the user image, because it ships no C library. The userland depends on the toolchain's libm for thirteen functions - pow, exp, log, log2, log10, sqrt, fmod, sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan2 - which newlib supplies from ARM's tarball. runtime/libc/math.c supplies only the six that are exact bit manipulation. Writing the missing thirteen by hand is not a tidy-up: a plausible wrong answer in a font rasteriser looks like a rendering bug rather than an arithmetic one. This is the shape of the question the Pi will ask, and it is not a HAL question."}, {"id": "docs_setup_no_linux_toolchain", "label": "Do not use aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Toolchain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It brings glibc, Linux start files and a dynamic loader, which is exactly what -ffreestanding -nostdlib -nostartfiles exists to avoid."}, {"id": "docs_setup_uart_debugging", "label": "Debugging without a debugger, over the UART", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Debugging", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A putchar that works from the third instruction is the first thing to build. When something hangs, instrument until you find the last line that executed - bisecting with puts is primitive and it is the fastest thing there is. On real hardware there is no GDB, only UART."}, {"id": "docs_setup_exception_handler", "label": "The exception handler that prints ESR, ELR and FAR", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Debugging", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The best investment in the project: it turns a silent hang into a message telling you which instruction faulted and on what address."}, {"id": "docs_setup_gdb_qemu", "label": "GDB against QEMU", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Debugging", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Earns its keep on context switch bugs, which are nearly impossible to find with prints."}, {"id": "docs_setup_dual_output", "label": "Output goes to serial and framebuffer at once", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Where output goes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When something breaks, the framebuffer breaks too: a page fault in the compositor leaves the screen frozen on the last frame. Serial takes a different path and keeps talking after everything else has died. Never turn the serial off."}, {"id": "docs_setup_upstream_lua_untouched", "label": "Never edit lua/upstream directly", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Upstream Lua", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Freestanding changes live in lua/patches and are applied during the build, so a new upstream version updates without fighting your own changes. Ten minutes now, a week later."}, {"id": "docs_setup_setjmp_longjmp", "label": "setjmp/longjmp demands the most care", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Upstream Lua", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lua uses it for error handling, and getting it wrong produces a bug that only shows up when something raises an error, long afterwards."}, {"id": "docs_setup_debug_uart_cable", "label": "3-pin JST-SH debug UART cable, pending", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Hardware pending", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It blocks the Pi 5 target. Until then, all work happens under QEMU."}, {"id": "docs_setup_9p_spec", "label": "The 9P spec", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Short, readable in an afternoon. The conceptual origin of the Kosmos protocol."}, {"id": "docs_setup_rust_rpi_tutorials", "label": "rust-raspberrypi-OS-tutorials (Andre Richter)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Andre Richter", "contributor": null, "rationale": "In Rust, but the Pi bring-up sequence is the best reference available."}, {"id": "docs_setup_osdev_wiki", "label": "The OSDev wiki", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_setup_haiku_source", "label": "The Haiku source", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For BeOS internals and app_server design."}, {"id": "docs_setup_sel4", "label": "seL4", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For thinking about IPC and capability design."}, {"id": "docs_setup_elua", "label": "eLua", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prior art for Lua on bare metal."}, {"id": "docs_setup_arm_arm", "label": "ARM Architecture Reference Manual (ARMv8-A)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The source of truth for exceptions, page tables and barriers."}, {"id": "docs_setup_bcm2712_datasheet", "label": "BCM2712 datasheet (Pi 5)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_setup_setup", "target": "docs_setup_arm_gnu_toolchain", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_arm_gnu_toolchain", "target": "docs_setup_libm_dependency", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_arm_gnu_toolchain", "target": "docs_setup_no_linux_toolchain", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_arm_gnu_toolchain", "target": "docs_setup_gatekeeper_quarantine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_default_is_the_machine_written_on", "target": "docs_setup_arm_gnu_toolchain", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_libm_dependency", "target": "docs_glossary_freestanding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_uart_debugging", "target": "docs_setup_exception_handler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_exception_handler", "target": "docs_glossary_esr_elr_far", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_uart_debugging", "target": "docs_setup_gdb_qemu", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_dual_output", "target": "docs_architecture_console_server", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_dual_output", "target": "docs_glossary_framebuffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_upstream_lua_untouched", "target": "docs_setup_setjmp_longjmp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_setjmp_longjmp", "target": "docs_glossary_longjmp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_setup", "target": "docs_setup_9p_spec", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference material", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_setup_setup", "target": "docs_setup_rust_rpi_tutorials", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/setup.md", "source_location": "Reference materi